---
title: 08 - Blynk and the web pages
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant OS as Online Server
  participant BL as Blynk cloud
  participant MP as Online web page, Monitor<br/>(owner, technician)
  participant CP as status.html<br/>(customer phone, QR sticker)
  participant AP as Blynk app<br/>(a phone)

  loop every 1 min (30 s to 1 h)
    OS->>BL: write the private device V0 (live JSON: the 3 boxes with step, time, coins, doors, helmet and relays, the Refilling Station's level of each main container with valve, waiting and failed, board flags, statistics, revenue)
    OS->>BL: write the public device V0 (per box: step, seconds left, main controller heard, session counter)
  end
  OS->>BL: a new alert: event 'alert' (out of order, Refilling Station offline, refill failed, board not heard)
  BL-->>AP: push notification (works with the page closed)

  loop every 10 s, only while the tab is open and visible
    MP->>BL: HTTPS GET the private V0 (token typed once, kept in that browser)
    BL-->>MP: the live JSON
    Note over MP: LIVE / DELAYED / OLD DATA, each box drawn as a little machine, three level dials from the Refilling Station (red EMPTY or LOW, yellow MID, green HIGH and MAX, waiting or refilling), network map, Alerts with sounds, Reports
  end

  loop every 30 s, only while the page is open and visible
    CP->>BL: HTTPS GET the public V0 (public token, in the QR code)
    BL-->>CP: step and seconds left of each box
    Note over CP: TAPS = FREE, other steps = IN USE with minutes left, OUT OF ORDER, NO INFORMATION
  end

  opt the customer types a nickname (only after the coins are in)
    CP->>BL: write V5: name, the box's session counter, time
    BL-->>CP: V5 is read back and shown on the box card
  end
  Note over CP,BL: the nickname disappears when the box's session counter changes (the cycle ended)
